# Phase 15b Backend Configuration
# Copy this to .env.local (local development) or configure these in Vercel dashboard

# ============================================================================
# Google OAuth2 Configuration
# ============================================================================
# Get these from: https://console.cloud.google.com/
#
# Steps:
# 1. Create a Google Cloud project
# 2. Enable Google Drive API
# 3. Create OAuth 2.0 credentials (Web application)
# 4. Set authorized redirect URIs:
#    - For local dev: http://localhost:5173 (Vite dev server)
#    - For production: https://yourdomain.com
# 5. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret here

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173

# ============================================================================
# CORS Configuration
# ============================================================================
# Controls which origins can call the /api/auth/* endpoints
# 
# Local development: http://localhost:5173 (Vite dev server)
# Production: https://yourdomain.com
# Multiple origins: separate with commas (app will check Origin header)

CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ============================================================================
# Security Notes
# ============================================================================
# - NEVER commit .env.local to git (already in .gitignore)
# - NEVER expose GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET in frontend code
# - NEVER log tokens or sensitive data
# - Always use HTTPS in production
# - Rotate CLIENT_SECRET regularly if compromised
# - Use Vercel's Environment Variables for production (encrypted at rest)

# ============================================================================
# Optional: Token Expiration Strategy
# ============================================================================
# These are handled by Google's OAuth2 response (typically 1 hour for access_token)
# The frontend (sync/auth.ts) schedules token refresh 30s before expiry
